<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly lower.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly lower.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly lower on Monday since banks expect a surge of peso liquidity this week from maturing T-bills and T-notes, dealers said.</p>
<p>Some 4.9 billion of pesos are estimated to have matured this Monday and another 5.1 billion to 3.6 billion pesos are seen to come in on Wednesday from maturing T-bills, traders said.</p>
<p>PHIBOR represents the rates at which banks are willing to swap their pesos for dollars.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  NOV 25		 NOV 24</p>
<p>    1 W		11  7/16		11  9/16</p>
<p>    2 W		11  7/16		11  5/8</p>
<p>    1 M		11  3/8		 11  7/16</p>
<p>    2 M		11  3/8		 11  7/16</p>
<p>    3 M		11  7/16		11  1/2</p>
<p>    6 M		11 11/16		11 11/16</p>
<p>    12M		11 13/16		11 13/16</p>
<p>    VAL		26-Nov		  25-Nov</p>
<p>-- LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
